seg-2172d9ea618e = The 16-parameter Keplerian set degrades from { "0.04" } cm at { "60" } s to { "9.35" } cm at { "900" } s: one Keplerian set with twice-per-revolution harmonics cannot follow the higher-frequency gravity terms and the drag of a LEO arc for more than a few minutes, and its least-squares residual oscillates across the window. The along/cross/radial polynomials (degrees { "7" }, { "5" }, { "6" }) absorb what is left: { "1.01" } cm at { "900" } s, { "0.21" } cm at { "600" } s. At the shortest intervals the Keplerian figures are sub-millimetre and no longer strictly ordered (the fit is then limited by conditioning, not by the model).

